1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,240
Pompeii got seventeen years of warnings,

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:03,840
and spent them fixing the roofs.

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:05,300
You see, in the year 62,

4
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:07,580
a huge earthquake wrecked the city.

5
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:08,140
The plan?

6
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:08,780
Rebuild.

7
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:09,520
Same spot.

8
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,060
The mountain above them was green and

9
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:11,900
covered in vineyards.

10
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,540
To them, it was just a mountain.

11
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:15,860
Then, in 79, the ground shook for

12
00:00:15,860 --> 00:00:16,200
days.

13
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:18,060
The locals shrugged: "Relax,

14
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,000
it's Campania.

15
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:20,040
It always shakes."

16
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:22,240
Around midday, the mountain exploded.

17
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:24,200
Across the bay, a teenager named Pliny

18
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:25,900
watched a cloud shaped like a giant

19
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,560
pine tree climb into the sky.

20
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:28,880
His uncle, an admiral,

21
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:30,860
grabbed the fleet and sailed straight toward

22
00:00:30,860 --> 00:00:31,660
it, to rescue people.

23
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:32,620
He never came back.

24
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:34,640
Over Pompeii, it started raining stones.

25
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:36,440
Light pumice, for hours.

26
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:38,220
And those freshly fixed roofs?

27
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:39,360
They caved in under the weight.

28
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:40,300
Many people ran.

29
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:42,180
Others hid indoors, waiting for it to

30
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:42,400
stop.

31
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:43,300
It didn't.

32
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:45,040
The next morning, an avalanche of scorching

33
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:46,900
gas and ash raced down the mountain,

34
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:48,280
faster than anyone could run.

35
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:49,820
You see, magma is like a shaken

36
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:50,160
soda.

37
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:51,780
Gas builds pressure for centuries,

38
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:52,620
then the cap pops,

39
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:54,000
and everything comes out at once.

40
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,660
Pompeii vanished so completely that in 1599,

41
00:00:57,880 --> 00:00:59,700
an architect dug a tunnel right through

42
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:01,300
it, and never realized.

43
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:03,320
Seventeen years fixing the roofs.

44
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:04,860
One day to lose them.

